.Dd November 19, 2026
.Dt SETTERM 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm setterm
.Nd set the console's blank time, or blank, unblank or ask it
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl -blank
.Op Ar minutes | Cm force | Cm poke
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sets how long the console waits without a key or a mouse move before it
blanks, as util-linux's
.Nm
does with the same option; see
.Xr console 4 .
A blank darkens the screen, turns every backlight off and turns the
console's display off, and the next key or mouse move undoes it.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -blank Ar minutes
Write the escape
.Li ESC [ 9 ; Ar minutes Li \&]
to the standard output: the console blanks after
.Ar minutes
without input, 0 to 60, and never for 0.
The count starts again, and a blank console is shown.
.It Fl -blank Cm force
Blank the console now, until
.Fl -blank Cm poke ;
a key does not end this blank.
When the console stays shown, as under a program's picture on
.Pa /fb
that neither a backlight nor a display driver can darken, it says so and
exits 1; util-linux's exits 0 there.
.It Fl -blank Cm poke
Unblank the console.
.It Fl -blank
Print 1 while the console is blank and 0 otherwise.
.El
.Pp
The option may be written
.Fl blank
or
.Fl -blank Ns = Ns Ar arg ,
as util-linux allows.
.Cm force ,
.Cm poke
and the question are TIOCLINUX requests on the standard input, which must
be the console, as on Linux.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 for a usage error, a time outside 0 to 60, a request
the console refused, or a
.Cm force
that left the console shown.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Blank the console after five minutes without input:
.Dl setterm --blank 5
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It setterm: blank: refused: nothing darkens the screen
.Cm force
left the console shown.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr term 1 ,
.Xr console 4
.Sh STANDARDS
util-linux's
.Nm
has many more options; this one has
.Fl -blank
alone, which BusyBox lacks.
Inside
.Xr term 1
the escape reaches term and not the console, and the TIOCLINUX requests
are refused, as on a Linux terminal emulator; the boot line's
.Li consoleblank=
sets the time there.
